IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III Reduction of Premium for Employers with Wage-Loss Plans:
-- regs 60, 61 and 62 (definition of "plan", application of the Part, and the reduction of the employer's premium rate).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Unofficial plain-text rendering; nothing here is "verified against the
-- official text". No section GIVEN: every rule has its own GIVEN.
--
-- THE RELATION. The employer's premium rate (Act s 68, out of range: section 68 of the Act, piece ei3) is reduced
-- for the insured persons covered by a plan that meets the standards of regs 63 to 66 and is a qualifying plan
-- (reg 67(3)); the insured persons must benefit from at least five-twelfths of the reduction (reg 61; Act s 69(1)(b),
-- out of range, piece ei3). Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a ratio or a rate is a fraction (0.5% is 0.005).

§ `Regulation 60 -- plan`

-- "includes" is read as: the four named kinds are plans whether or not the text elsewhere calls them wage-loss plans
-- covering insured persons; any other plan must be a wage-loss plan that covers insured persons employed by an
-- employer (fork F3).
-- src:1012 | 60 The definition in this section applies to this Part.
-- src:1013 | plan means a wage-loss plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer, and includes a Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan and an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan referred to in sections 63, 64, 65 and 66, respectively. (régime)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 60 (src:1012-1013)
GIVEN kind IS A `er4 Kind of wage-loss plan`
      `a wage-loss plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 60 plan` IF
        `a wage-loss plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer`
    OR  (NOT (kind EQUALS `er4 another wage-loss plan`))

§ `Regulation 61 -- when this Part applies`

-- src:1016 | 61 This Part applies where insured persons, who are employed by an employer and are covered by a plan that meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66, benefit from a reduction of the employer's premium in an amount at least equal to five-twelfths of the reduction.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 61 (src:1016)
GIVEN reduction IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 61 five-twelfths of the reduction of the employer's premium` MEANS
    (reduction TIMES 5) DIVIDED BY 12

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 61 (src:1016)
GIVEN `insured persons employed by an employer are covered by a plan that meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction of the employer's premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the reduction that the insured persons benefit from` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 61 this Part applies` IF
        `insured persons employed by an employer are covered by a plan that meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66`
    AND `the amount of the reduction that the insured persons benefit from`
            AT LEAST `reg 61 five-twelfths of the reduction of the employer's premium` `the reduction of the employer's premium`

§ `Regulation 62 -- reduction of the employer's premium rate`

§§ `Regulation 62(1) -- the reduction`

-- "By the percentage by which (a) is less than (b)": read as the relative shortfall, (b minus a) over b, so that
-- an experience cost ratio of 0.8% against a first payer cost ratio of 1.0% is a reduction of 20% of the rate
-- (fork F4). If (a) is not less than (b) there is no reduction, and if (b) is not above zero the percentage is not
-- defined: NOTHING.
-- src:1019 | 62 (1) Subject to subsection (2), an employer's premium rate fixed under section 68 of the Act shall be reduced, in respect of insured persons employed by that employer who are covered by a plan that meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66 and is a qualifying plan pursuant to subsection 67(3), by the percentage by which
-- src:1020 | (a) the experience cost ratio calculated under subsection (3) in respect of each category of insured persons covered by such a plan
-- src:1021 | is less than
-- src:1022 | (b) the first payer cost ratio calculated under subsection (4) for all insured persons.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 62(1) (src:1019-1022)
GIVEN `the experience cost ratio` IS A NUMBER
      `the first payer cost ratio` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 62(1) the percentage by which the experience cost ratio is less than the first payer cost ratio` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the first payer cost ratio` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
           IF `the experience cost ratio` AT LEAST `the first payer cost ratio` THEN JUST 0
           OTHERWISE JUST ((`the first payer cost ratio` MINUS `the experience cost ratio`) DIVIDED BY `the first payer cost ratio`)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 62(1) (src:1019-1022)
GIVEN `the employer's premium rate fixed under section 68 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      percentage IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate reduced by the percentage` MEANS
    `the employer's premium rate fixed under section 68 of the Act` TIMES (1 MINUS percentage)

-- The reduction is "in respect of insured persons ... covered by a plan that meets the requirements of section 63, 64,
-- 65 or 66 and is a qualifying plan pursuant to subsection 67(3)", and "subject to subsection (2)".
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 62(1) (src:1019-1022)
GIVEN `the insured person is covered under a plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan is a qualifying plan pursuant to subsection 67(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligibility to use days of paid sick leave is deferred under a plan that meets the requirements of section 65 or 66` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate is to be reduced in respect of the insured person` IF
        `the insured person is covered under a plan`
    AND `the plan meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66`
    AND `the plan is a qualifying plan pursuant to subsection 67(3)`
    AND (NOT `reg 62(2) the employer's premium rate is not to be reduced in respect of the insured person`
                `the insured person is covered under a plan`
                `the plan meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66`
                `eligibility to use days of paid sick leave is deferred under a plan that meets the requirements of section 65 or 66`)

§§ `Regulation 62(2) -- when the rate is not reduced`

-- src:1023 | (2) An employer's premium rate fixed under section 68 of the Act shall not be reduced in respect of
-- src:1024 | (a) an insured person who is not covered under a plan;
-- src:1025 | (b) an insured person who is covered under a plan that does not meet the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66; or
-- src:1026 | (c) an insured person whose eligibility to use days of paid sick leave is deferred under a plan that meets the requirements of section 65 or 66.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 62(2) (src:1023-1026)
GIVEN `the insured person is covered under a plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligibility to use days of paid sick leave is deferred under a plan that meets the requirements of section 65 or 66` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 62(2) the employer's premium rate is not to be reduced in respect of the insured person` IF
        (NOT `the insured person is covered under a plan`)
    OR  (`the insured person is covered under a plan` AND (NOT `the plan meets the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66`))
    OR  `eligibility to use days of paid sick leave is deferred under a plan that meets the requirements of section 65 or 66`

§§ `Regulation 62(3) -- the experience cost ratio`

-- "The three years ending concurrently with the second year preceding the year for which the calculation is made":
-- for the year Y they are Y-4, Y-3 and Y-2.
-- src:1031 | with both averages being taken over the three years ending concurrently with the second year preceding the year for which the calculation is made.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 62(3) (src:1031)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`reg 62(3) the three years over which both averages are taken` MEANS
    LIST (year MINUS 4), (year MINUS 3), (year MINUS 2)

-- The Commission divides (a) the average cost of benefits paid under section 12 and paragraph 18(1)(b) of the Act to
-- insured persons whose interruption of earnings was by reason of illness, injury or quarantine by (b) the average
-- amount of the yearly insurable earnings for the insured persons, both averages over those three years, for each
-- category of insured persons covered by plans that meet the requirements. The yearly figures are inputs
-- (out of range: sections 12 and 18(1)(b) of the Act, piece ei1). Anything but three yearly figures of each kind, or
-- average earnings that are not above zero, is not covered: NOTHING.
-- src:1027 | (3) For the purpose of determining the experience cost ratio for a year, the Commission shall, in respect of each category of insured persons covered by plans that meet the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66, divide
-- src:1028 | (a) the average cost of benefits paid under section 12 and paragraph 18(1)(b) of the Act to insured persons whose interruption of earnings was by reason of illness, injury or quarantine
-- src:1029 | by
-- src:1030 | (b) the average amount of the yearly insurable earnings for the insured persons,
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 62(3) (src:1027-1030)
GIVEN `the yearly cost of benefits paid in each of the three years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the yearly insurable earnings in each of the three years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 62(3) the experience cost ratio` MEANS
    IF     count `the yearly cost of benefits paid in each of the three years` EQUALS 3
       AND count `the yearly insurable earnings in each of the three years` EQUALS 3
       AND sum `the yearly insurable earnings in each of the three years` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (sum `the yearly cost of benefits paid in each of the three years` DIVIDED BY sum `the yearly insurable earnings in each of the three years`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 62(4) -- the first payer cost ratio`

-- Same arithmetic, but for all insured persons and with the Commission's estimate of the cost that benefits would
-- have had if benefits payable under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan or paid sick leave plan
-- were disregarded. The estimate is the Commission's, so it is an input.
-- src:1032 | (4) For the purpose of determining the first payer cost ratio for a year, the Commission shall, in respect of all insured persons, divide
-- src:1033 | (a) the average cost of benefits that would have been paid under section 12 and paragraph 18(1)(b) of the Act to insured persons whose interruption of earnings was by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, as estimated by the Commission, if benefits payable under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan or paid sick leave plan were disregarded for the purpose of determining benefits otherwise payable to persons under the Act,
-- src:1034 | by
-- src:1035 | (b) the average of the yearly insurable earnings for the insured persons,
-- src:1036 | with both averages being taken over the three years ending concurrently with the second year preceding the year for which the calculation is made.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 62(4) (src:1032-1036)
GIVEN `the Commission's estimate of the yearly cost of benefits in each of the three years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the yearly insurable earnings of all insured persons in each of the three years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 62(4) the first payer cost ratio` MEANS
    IF     count `the Commission's estimate of the yearly cost of benefits in each of the three years` EQUALS 3
       AND count `the yearly insurable earnings of all insured persons in each of the three years` EQUALS 3
       AND sum `the yearly insurable earnings of all insured persons in each of the three years` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (sum `the Commission's estimate of the yearly cost of benefits in each of the three years` DIVIDED BY sum `the yearly insurable earnings of all insured persons in each of the three years`)
    ELSE NOTHING
